          "eval_mode": "substring",
          "prediction": "To identify the activist and the person who visited and naturalized in the kingdom, we need to consider the historical context of colonization and independence movements in the 20th century. We should focus on a specific country that was colonized, had notable independence activists, and was annexed by another country. Additionally, we need to find a documentary from the 1990s to 2000s that features the first person to visit and naturalize in the kingdom related to the independence activist. \n\n1. Identify a colonized country that was annexed in the 20th century.\n2. Research notable independence activists from that country between 1900 and 1950.\n3. Find out which activist was sent to promote independence in another country.\n4. Look for a person from the country where the activist was sent who visited and naturalized in the kingdom.\n5. Identify the documentary produced between 1990 and 2000 that depicts this person and find out who acted as them. \n\nThis structured approach will help narrow down the possibilities and lead to the final answer.",
